"}],"maturity":"post_opinion","official_detail_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcript/2020","official_disposition_urls":["https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/20pdf/594us2r62_19m1.pdf"],"official_docket_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/docket/docketfiles/html/public/19-1039.html","primary_docket":"19-1039","revisions":[{"correction_note":"Rewritten to the concise citizen-facing editorial standard.","created_at":"2026-08-30T17:07:43.591431Z","maturity":"post_opinion","revision_number":1}],"schema_version":"1.0","sections":[{"heading":"What this case is about","paragraphs":["PennEast Pipeline wants to build a gas line. It needs land in New Jersey. The company sued in federal court. New Jersey refused to comply. The state claims the Eleventh Amendment bars the suit. PennEast argues federal law overrides state immunity. The Court must decide if private parties can sue states for land."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 34, lines 45-49","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 34, lines 45-49"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 23-27","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 23-27"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 54, lines 45-39","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 54, lines 45-39"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 67, lines 53-55","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 67, lines 53-55"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 93, lines 19-11","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 93, lines 19-11"}]},{"heading":"How the case got here","paragraphs":["The Supreme Court heard oral argument in this case on April 28, 2021."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 11-21","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 11-21"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 66, lines 7-51","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 66, lines 7-51"}]},{"heading":"What each side wants","paragraphs":["PennEast wants the Court to allow the federal lawsuit to proceed.","New Jersey wants the Court to dismiss the case based on state immunity."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 34, lines 45-49","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 34, lines 45-49"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 23-27","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 23-27"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 54, lines 45-39","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 54, lines 45-39"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 67, lines 53-55","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 67, lines 53-55"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 93, lines 19-11","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 93, lines 19-11"}]},{"heading":"What each side says","paragraphs":["PennEast argues federal law deputizes private companies to exercise eminent domain.","New Jersey argues the Eleventh Amendment bars private suits against states."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 34, lines 45-49","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 34, lines 45-49"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 23-27","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 23-27"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 54, lines 45-39","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 54, lines 45-39"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 67, lines 53-55","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 67, lines 53-55"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 93, lines 19-11","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2020/19-1039_o7jq.pdf","page_label":"file page 93, lines 19-11"}]},{"heading":"What the justices asked","paragraphs":["Justice Alito asked if state immunity was part of the union bargain.","Justice Thomas asked how deputizing differs from delegating power to private parties."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Tra